---
import Deliberation from './Deliberation.astro';
---

<section id="work" class="section work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
  <h2 id="work-title" class="section-title">Work</h2>

  <article class="item grid-12">
    <div class="item__head">
      <h3>A panel of AI agents that has to agree before you get an answer</h3>
      <p class="meta">Einstein Industries. Designed and built alone.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item__body body-copy">
      <p>
        It started with a problem in legal work: nobody trusts a single model's answer, and they shouldn't. So a chair
        agent gathers the context around a question first. The stakes, the values in play, how confident the answer
        needs to be. Then it briefs a panel of sandboxed models from different providers. They draft. The chair merges.
        They vote, and one dissent sends it back for another round.
      </p>
      <p>Any agent can raise its hand and ask the operator a question. It's slow on purpose.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item__figure"><Deliberation /></div>
  </article>

  <article class="item grid-12">
    <div class="item__head">
      <p class="item__figure-number math" aria-hidden="true">10×</p>
      <h3><span class="visually-hidden">10× </span>throughput on client work, from one MCP server</h3>
      <p class="meta">Einstein Industries. One of two developers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item__body body-copy">
      <p>
        Built on FastMCP. Its tools reach into every app in our suite, pull a client's whole history, and assemble a
        working model of the finished product. People review it and push back instead of starting from a blank page.
        Work that took other departments days of manual digging now starts from a draft. We measured before and after.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="item grid-12">
    <div class="item__head">
      <h3>Retiring a login system from 2012</h3>
      <p class="meta">Einstein Industries. Me and the sysadmin.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="item__body body-copy">
      <p>Cognito with Google sign-in across the whole suite of applications.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

</section>

<style>
  .item {
    padding-block: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    row-gap: 20px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .item__head {
    grid-column: span 5;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .item__body {
    grid-column: 7 / span 6;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .item__figure {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 36px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .item__figure-number {
    font-size: 88px;
    line-height: 0.9;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .item__head,
    .item__body {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
